		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Featherstone articulated body algorithm]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=389#p389"><![CDATA[
Hi Niels,<br>  Are you forgetting maybe to add the gravity force to your base link? <br><br>mLinks[h]-&gt;ZA_s should be initialized with -g_h (spatial gravity force in the local h coordinate frame) before you loop through the children of h to add their contributions.   That term should, I believe, cancel out the contribution from  (mLinks<em class="text-italics">-&gt;csu/mLinks<em class="text-italics">-&gt;csd) * mLinks<em class="text-italics">-&gt;csh )) as mLinks<em class="text-italics">-&gt;csu = -s_i * g_i  . <br><br>I find it easier to troubleshoot Featherstone's algorithm when I look at the equations in pseudo-code form.  If you take a look here:<br><br><a href="http://research.scea.com/research/pdfs/VangelisK_GDC2004.pdf" class="postlink">http://research.scea.com/research/pdfs/ ... DC2004.pdf</a><br><br>on page 4 you'll find a more compact representation of the loops involved in Featherstone's algorithm.<br><br>Hope this helps...<br><br>Cheers,<br>Vangelis</em></em></em></em><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=329">vangelis</a> — Tue Oct 18, 2005 5:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
